{
  "rationale": "The plant automata G model the robot's perception (obstacle and marker detection) and its motion capabilities. The specification automata E encode the safe, efficient search and approach policy: always avoid obstacles, switch to marker tracking when marker_seen, approach until marker_close, and stop at the goal. Recovery from obstacles is deterministic and always passes through a scan/search state before resuming exploration.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate plant automata for perception (G1) and motion (G2) to modularize sensing and actuation.",
    "Specification automata (E1, E2, E3) bind perception outcomes to safe/goal-seeking actions, enforce deterministic obstacle recovery, marker tracking, and terminal stop at the goal."
  ],
